---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import DraftNotice from "../components/DraftNotice.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What this site does and does not collect."
>
  <DraftNotice
    note="This Privacy page is a draft and has not yet been reviewed by an insurance-regulatory or privacy lawyer. It describes this site as it works today and will be updated if that changes."
  />
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      This site is currently built to collect as little as possible. This
      page describes what actually happens today, not a general privacy
      policy template.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site does not collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No accounts or sign-ups</li>
      <li>No lead forms or contact forms</li>
      <li>No document or file uploads</li>
      <li>No cookies, and nothing stored in your browser</li>
      <li>No analytics or tracking of what you type or click</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The Coverage Gap Checker and other tools</h2>
    <p>
      Numbers you type into a tool on this site — like the
      <a href="/tools/">Coverage Gap Checker</a> — are used only in your
      browser, on your device, to calculate the results you see. They are
      never sent to a server, never saved, and never seen by us. Closing or
      refreshing the page clears everything you entered.
    </p>

    <h2>If this changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we ever add something that does collect information — an account
      system, a contact form, analytics, or a lead/referral feature — this
      page will be updated first to describe exactly what's collected, why,
      and how it's used, and that feature will go through legal review before
      launch. See <a href="/how-we-make-money/">How We Make Money</a> for
      what future features we might consider.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>[Contact details to be added once a legal entity and contact process are established.]</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
